36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've found that past joint ventures and home visits have struggled. One joint clinic closed because of rota and budget disputes, and a shared nursing round had a very high failure rate for visits.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My research shows that a previous call-back trial successfully reduced readmissions for elderly patients, though the benefit vanished once it ended. Also, our booking system only records fixed slots, meaning unbooked work is effectively invisible.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The staffing situation is concerning. We have significant nursing vacancies and a loss of physiotherapists to the city, though the midwifery rota currently has unusual slack. We must be careful not to overstretch the already burdened teams.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The financial outlook is bleak. Our development budget is down by a quarter, and we're now paying for floor space from it. Furthermore, any program operating off-site earns us nothing from the regional fund.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have many hurdles. Our rooms and parking are already at capacity by mid-morning, and the shuttle reaches so few villages. We must be very careful about adding more traffic to our site.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, since off-site work earns nothing and @Shizue mentioned our site is full, we are in a difficult position. We need a program that is financially viable but doesn't seize up our physical space.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, that is a fair point. However, we must also consider that the call-back trial proved that proactive follow-up actually works for patients. We shouldn't ignore efficacy just because the logistics are difficult.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, efficacy is important, but not if it relies on staff we don't have. With nursing vacancies rising and physiotherapists leaving, we cannot afford a program that adds pressure to those specific groups.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, then the logic is simple. We need a program that utilizes the ""slack"" you mentioned in the midwifery rota and stays on-site to ensure we actually bill the regional fund. Anything else is a financial drain.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I agree that we must be mindful of the budget and our space. If we can find a program that uses existing slack and doesn't overcrowd our parking or rooms, that would be ideal.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, your logic is sound. If we avoid off-site visits to ensure funding and avoid overstretching the nursing and therapy teams, we can find a sustainable path. I'm worried about joint ventures, though.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, I understand your concern about joint ventures, but we must weigh that against the proven benefit of follow-up care. If we can find a way to structure it sustainably, the patient outcome is worth the effort.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, the ""proven benefit"" doesn't help if the staff are too exhausted to deliver it. We cannot ignore the nursing vacancies. Any program relying on ward nurses or physiotherapists is a risk to our current stability.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, your idealism is touching, but irrelevant if the program collapses in a year. We need a solution that is fiscally responsible and staff-compatible. The midwifery slack is the only logical resource we have left.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, you make a strong point. If we can find a program that utilizes that slack without adding to the congestion of our parking and rooms, it would be the most considerate choice for everyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree. We need a program that is realistic about our budget and staffing. I'm hopeful that when we see the candidates, one will fit these constraints without repeating the mistakes of our past joint ventures.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. While I still believe patient outcomes should be our primary guide, I acknowledge that a program is only as good as its ability to survive the first year. Let us see the candidates.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. We must prioritize a program that doesn't exacerbate our staffing crisis. I will be looking for an option that avoids adding pressure to the nursing and therapy teams.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Let's be clear: we are looking for a program that is on-site for the funding, avoids the nursing and therapy deficits, and utilizes the midwifery slack. Anything else is just a fantasy. I'm ready to vote.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Let us hope the candidates offer a path that is gentle on our staff and practical for our facilities. I look forward to seeing the options.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
